      "Price moving between a HTF discount array and a HTF premium array",
      "Economic news drivers to deliver expansion volatility"
    ]
  },
  "glossary": {
    "CONTEXT": "Understanding where a market maker model will form based on price moving from a higher-timeframe discount array to a premium array; can be established with as few as two HTF candles.",
    "ST": "Sharp turn; an early entry signal marked by the first fair value gap forming off a HTF PD array, indicating that an intermediate term low/high has formed.",
    "SHORT_TERM_RANGE": "A directional swing containing a fair value gap, ideally originating from a discount/premium array, that acts as dynamic protection and provides an entry zone.",
    "MAGNET_AND_ROCKET": "A higher-timeframe fair value gap that first pulls price toward it like a magnet, and then rapidly rejects price away like a rocket upon mitigation."
  },
